<title>HONG KONG: HK domestic textile exports down 3.0 pct 1st qtr.</title>
<headline>HK domestic textile exports down 3.0 pct 1st qtr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic exports of textiles were down three percent year on year to HK$7.7 billion in the first quarter of 1997, the Census and Statistics Department said on Friday.</p>
<p>Domestic exports of consumer electrical and electronic products decreased by nine percent to HK$5.8 billion.</p>
<p>Machinery, equipment, apparatus, parts and components fell six percent year on year to HK$8.8 billion and wearing apparel was down four percent to HK$8.2 billion.</p>
<p>The four major industries accounted for 69 percent of Hong Kong's total domestic exports of manufactured goods in the first quarter of 1997, the department said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
